From: Nipuna H Herath <nipunaherath@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:19:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] CUDA/HIP: one kernel for a gated mix driven by two
 small products on one vector

MUL_MAT(W_f, g), MUL_MAT(W_g, g), TANH, MUL(., cur), SUB(cur, .), TANH,
MUL(msg, .), ADD = cur - tanh(W_f g)*cur + msg*tanh(W_g g), view nodes allowed
between, runs as one kernel with a warp per output row (Inkling 2 loop
controllers: 64-long g, 2304 rows, 96 per token). F32/F16/BF16 weights, one
token, intermediate results used only inside.

R9700 Inkling-2-Mini UD-Q8_K_XL tg128 46.3 -> 48.6 tok/s, 3078 -> 2699
kernels per token. New test-backend-ops case CTRL_MIX.
